<title>USA: TWA to discontinue cargo fuel surcharges.</title>
<headline>TWA to discontinue cargo fuel surcharges.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Friday it was discontinuing its domestic cargo fuel surcharge, implemented late last year, effective today.</p>
<p>The carrier said it initiated the surcharge after fuel prices rose for 14 oconsecutive weeks.</p>
<p>TWA said a recent fuel price decline had lasted long enough so that it could discontinue the charge of $0.025 per pound of shipped goods.</p>
<p>TWA plans to eliminate the international fuel surcharge of $0.06 per kilogram as of May 1.</p>
<p>TWA is the seventh-largest U.S. passenger carrier.</p>
<p>Its shares were unchanged at 6-5/8.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
